(Title) Tj
T*
(Multimodal Neuroimaging Integration Does Not Enhance Motor Interface Performance in) Tj
T*
(Healthy Learners) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Abstract) Tj
T*
(The combination of scalp electroencephalography and near-infrared spectroscopy was) Tj
T*
(hypothesized to improve brain-machine interface control fidelity compared to) Tj
T*
(electroencephalography alone. Sixteen healthy participants completed five standardized) Tj
T*
(motor control training sessions using either single-source \(electroencephalography-only\)) Tj
T*
(or dual-source \(electroencephalography plus near-infrared spectroscopy\) signal) Tj
T*
(interpretation systems. Classification recall measured in real-time during three-class) Tj
T*
(motor tasks averaged 58.2% in the electroencephalography-only condition and 54.1% in the) Tj
T*
(multimodal condition \(p = 0.34\). Agency perception, quantified on standardized scales,) Tj
T*
(approached 73% of maximum in both groups \(p = 0.61\). Computational optimization identified) Tj
T*
(fronto-central electrode placement as most informative across both modalities, while near-) Tj
T*
(infrared sensor positioning required individual-level calibration. Post-hoc simulation) Tj
T*
(analysis indicated comparable predictive utility between modalities. These findings) Tj
T*
(suggest that within standard classification and fusion methodologies, additional) Tj
T*
(neuroimaging channels do not confer performance advantage during acute training periods.) Tj
ET
